Attempt 3 closes the one open minor from the check. Comment lines were edited in place and never rewrapped, which left them over the package's 80-column width. Fixing the class meant rewrapping every comment line in the package that ran over 80 columns, plus every file reference split across two comment lines by in-place edits. Only comments changed (the before-and-after diff touches no code). Members fixed together:
(a) doc.go "Every $schema is checked wherever the library may read it..." (old line 76, 89 cols): lines 75-79 reflowed locally into 75-80;
(b) doc.go "The compiled graph, every schema the library compiled..." (old line 269, 135 cols): reflowed into lines 270-271;
(c) schema.go compilePrepared doc comment (line 242, 82 cols): rewrapped;
(d) annotation_test.go TestHandleFrozenEngine doc comment (line 521, 105 cols): rewrapped, and the split reference "objcompiler.go\n// :188-192" joined into "objcompiler.go:188-192";
(e) a sibling of the split reference, compiled.go visitCompiled doc comment "(compiler.go:\n// 153-157, 190-214)": joined into "compiler.go:153-157, 190-214" and rewrapped.
After the change, the awk width check lists only regexcost_test.go:623, the //nolint directive that predates this work (it is identical at HEAD e1e9657).
The GC-21 class fix from attempts 1 and 2 is unchanged:
(1) the inspector refuses a compiled Format, ContentEncoding, ContentMediaType or ContentSchema at its keyword (inspect.go refuseAssertions);
(2) the per-compile regexpEngine is frozen when compileWith or compileWalked returns, whatever the outcome; its cache is dropped, and later calls fail with errEngineFrozen and cache nothing (schema.go);
(3) every schema the library compiled is listed (compiled.go compiledSchemas). The walk's $schema rule then applies at each listed position the walk did not walk (checkCollected), and every compiled schema is inspected and analyzed, the $dynamicAnchor schemas included (visitCompiled, inspectCompiled);
(4) doc.go now says format and content stay annotations because of these refusals, not only because AssertFormat and AssertContent are unset.
I ran every mutation proof again in this attempt with go test -overlay. Mutants are under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/wp51close/g01/mut/.

Verdict: fix, for three minor test gaps. GC-01's behavior is bounded and correct; I found no blocker or major.

**Behavior.** I ran every round-9 shape and the hostile input from each P, C1, C2, C3, V1 and V2 row through compileRaw (spy loader), Check, Factory.Build and Handle, each once with $recursiveRef and once as its $ref twin. Probe: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/wp51close/g02check2/probe/shapes.txt.
- 56 shapes were refused with findings identical to the twin's: same pointers, no panic, the loader never asked, all within 35 ms and 12 MB.
  - round-9 shapes (1) to (6), among them the type bomb, allOf of 300 minimum, seven 400x patterns, allOf of 40,000, 12,000 properties, https and file URLs, and additionalItems multipleOf 0;
  - the VLU-16, VLU-51 and VLU-52 literals;
  - the CMP-31 and CMP-35 targets, REFS-12, REFS-13 and REFS-31;
  - every CX-04 $recursiveAnchor route;
  - 20 same-root-cause variants not in the audit (chained and deep targets, sites inside a live additionalItems, anchor and $id routes, embedded-resource bases, dependentSchemas, not, if, items array, definitions, dependencies).
- I found no unlisted escaping path. Shapes where $recursiveAnchor true sits on an ancestor that is not a schema compile, but that ancestor is never compiled, so the target stays static.

**Pre-fix proof.** I built an overlay that reverts every GC-01 change, keeping G01's: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/wp51close/g02check2/pre/overlay.json.
- 195 GC-01 subtests fail on it. Every TestRecursiveRefRefusedByWalk row and all four new VAL-49 additionalItems twins fail.
- The rows that pass pre-fix are the pins the engineer named: meta-schema zero multipleOf, the $recursiveAnchor rows, additionalItems anchor and resource, cycle, doubling. The draft-07 and meta/core targets also pass, because G01's checkCollected refuses them, but RefusedByWalk still fails on them.
- The deviation marking zero multipleOf at an unknown-keyword target 'wrong' is correct. The library's meta-check of a $recursiveRef target refuses it at HEAD.

**Mutants.** I ran 46 mutants (the earlier checker's K01 to K30, plus my N01 to N17). All are killed except:
- the three in the findings: N07, N15 and N17;
- the equivalent mutants K23 and N11;
- K29, which only the full suite kills (TestInspectCompiledFailsClosed).

K26 and K27 are now killed by TestCompiledNumberWork, and K09 by TestInPlaceCycles, TestWorkCharges and TestRecursiveRefCharges.

The engineer's claim that K23 (loadIssues skips $recursiveRef) is killed is wrong. It survives the suite: checkRef refuses every such site before loadIssues can run, so the mutant cannot change behavior. Its earlier "kills" came only from the load-dependent heap tests TestHandleUnevaluatedBranches and TestHandleReservesDecodedMaps. The code needs no change.

**Checks.**
- Pass:
  - go build and go vet;
  - go test -race -cover -shuffle=on (324 s, 98.1% coverage);
  - the GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8 GOEXPERIMENT=jsonv2 floor;
  - golangci-lint run (0 issues) and golangci-lint fmt --diff (empty);
  - go run ./internal/tool/repocheck;
  - FuzzCompileSchema, FuzzCompilePattern, FuzzValidate and FuzzDifferential, 75 s each. I ran them in a scratch copy of the repo so no crasher could land in testdata.
- Fail: CGO_ENABLED=0 go test, twice, at load averages up to 19. Both times only TestHandleUnevaluatedBranches/unevaluatedItems failed, on a sampled heap peak. This is class GC-08 (audit CX-13), not a GC-01 regression. Run back to back, the tree and the pre-fix overlay gave the same reservation (5,029,320) and similar peaks.

**Housekeeping.** I modified no repository file: the package checksums match the start, and the untracked set is unchanged. All probes and overlays are under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/wp51close/g02check2/.

Attempt 3 for G02 (GC-01) closes the check's three open minors. Each fix covers the whole class, and production code is unchanged. Only tests and one doc.go paragraph changed. Every class member was proved by a mutation battery of 26 mutants, each run against the full package suite twice: once with the test files from the check's start state (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/758d7ca3-81cf-5fbc-a967-12d97bce3d6b/scratchpad/wp51close/g02a3/pre, md5 1275904d... and ed8a63c7..., matching the check's md5-start) and once with the new ones. Ten mutants survived the old suite (A03, B01, B02, C01-C07), and all 26 are killed now.

(1) The referenceKeywords sites, a class of 17 members (N15 was one). The class is every member of referenceKeywords() at every site that loops over it, plus each compiledReference case and each per-keyword runtime site.
- schema_test.go TestFanOut gains the row 'fan-out through a dynamic reference', expecting /allOf.
- recursive_test.go TestReferenceKeywords now checks, for every keyword in the list:
  - that edges() of {kw:'#/zz',zz:{...}} gives exactly one edge named kw, with no sub, factor 1 and its child at /zz;
  - that the walk records one site at /kw with the value '#/zz' and walks /zz live, with no issues.
- A sub-list at any site now fails for each member: edges (A01-A03), walk sites (A04-A06), isReference (A07-A09), compiledReference cases (A10-A12), work.go in-place edges (A13, A14) and keywords() units (A15-A17). The doc comment of TestReferenceKeywords says so.

(2) The exponentUpTo clamp, a class of 2 members (N07 plus the clamp tested before the step). TestCompiledNumberWork now pins the saturated charge numberUnits + len(lit)*numberByteUnits + numberExpUnits*countCap for six exponents:
- 1e18446744073709551616, which wraps to 0;
- 1e18446744073709551617, which wraps to 1;
- 1e9300000000000000000, which wraps negative;
- 1e99999999999999999999, the old row;
- -1e-18446744073709551617, the same with a negative sign;
- 1E+9300000000000000000, with an upper-case E and a plus sign.
It also asserts that exponentUpTo(1e18446744073709551617, MaxNumberExponent) equals the limit, which kills a clamp checked before the step (that variant returns 1844).

(3) The decision-pass group of every reference keyword and applicator in errorUnits, a class of 7 members (N17 was one). The members are $ref in the ref group, and $recursiveRef, $dynamicRef, not, allOf, anyOf and oneOf in the cond group. The new recursive_test.go TestDecisionPassOrder has one subtest per keyword, each sitting beside minLength 3:
- It pins the library's order (validator.go:148-175) with a probe format that counts calls. The decision pass, through the decideURL 'not' wrapper, calls the target at "a" only for $ref, and at "abc" for every keyword. The location pass calls it at both bodies.
- It pins the model at "a": decide is 3*decideErrorBytes (312) for $ref and decideErrorBytes (104) for every other keyword; locate is 2*errorBytes for all seven. Moving any one keyword between the groups fails that keyword's subtest.

The TestRecursiveRefCharges comment is reworded as the check asked. The charges equal the $ref twin's only when no keyword sits beside the reference, because the library evaluates $recursiveRef with $dynamicRef and the applicators after the value's own keywords, and its decision pass skips them once one of those failed. The doc.go 'Work bound' bullet on the decision pass's error tree now states the same exclusion and cites TestDecisionPassOrder.

The fixes of G01 and of G02 attempts 1 and 2 are untouched. The comment-width check lists only the earlier regexcost_test.go:623 nolint directive.
